<p>He was born on the same day as George Washington.
His occupation was farming.
<p>He married Rebeckah Davis and they moved to Brimfield, Mass., where most
of their children were born. His widow married a man by the name of Sherman. She died at Oswego, New York, in 1831, age 99 years.

<p> <b>References:</b>

<p>
Genealogical data gathered over a period of twenty-five years, from 1903 to
1923, by Richard H. Stephens, son of Ruby Ann Bishop Stevens; Edward S.
Bishop of Oswego, New York; Charles L. Bishop of Winona, Minnesota;
and Loren Clark Bishop of Douglas Wyoming.
